other ai/

# CI artifact staging (night-zen-1 hotfix, the .auto-update leak
# class): the maintenance workflow's download-artifact step must land
# its staging directory outside the work tree (RUNNER_TEMP), but this
# ignore line is the second wall - an in-tree staging directory named
# .auto-update can never ride a commit even if a future edit moves
# the download back in-tree.
.auto-update/

# Python bytecode (night-dragon-maintenance-T1, the zelynic
# root-owned __pycache__ class): the interpreter writes caches beside
# imported sources with the invoking user's ownership; a root-run
# harness leaves root-owned .pyc files a later non-root teardown
# cannot remove. Ignored at both shapes - the directory and the
# bare file.
__pycache__/
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local release-rehearsal staging (night-cafe-1, the sibling's
# release.yml "Prepare release artifacts" class): a release flow run
# outside CI builds its artifacts in dist/; staging is a product of
# the machine, never a commit.
dist/

# The night-cafe-1 vendored fixed CLI (scripts/labs-exp/, the
# sibling's labs-exp law): a locally built or patched zejtron binary
# is an extraction product of the machine, never a tracked file. The
# tracked lane is the packaged pair - the .gz archive and its .b3sum
# sidecar, produced by scripts/package/pack-local.sh and verified by
# `b3sum -c` on extraction. The raw name class is ignored at any
# suffix shape (a bare binary, a .o, a .exe) so a future hardening
# drop cannot ride a commit, while the .gz and .b3sum sidecars of the
# same name stay trackable - the archive bytes are what another
# machine verifies, the raw bytes are what this machine runs.
scripts/labs-exp/zejtron-fixed-*
!scripts/labs-exp/zejtron-fixed-*.gz
!scripts/labs-exp/zejtron-fixed-*.b3sum
